n8n vs. LangGraph: the split\
n8n handles the deterministic plumbing, the same role it already proved out on TraxSail:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Tenant intake webhook (the form we just built posts here)\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Session auth, login, CRUD endpoints for the property/unit/vendor/resident data\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Scheduled jobs, follow-up timers, SMS/email sending (Twilio/Resend)\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Deterministic vendor-matching math (avg response time, cost, completion rate, same pattern as TraxSail's reliability score, plain SQL, no AI call)\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Billing, notifications, the dashboard data endpoints\
{\listtext	\'95	}LangGraph handles the actual reasoning, the part that's genuinely stateful and branching:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reading a tenant's raw description and classifying category, urgency, and likely responsibility (owner vs. tenant)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The multi-step maintenance lifecycle as one continuous "thread": diagnose \uc0\u8594  find vendor \u8594  get quote \u8594  pause for human approval if over the cost threshold \u8594  resume \u8594  dispatch \u8594  follow up \u8594  verify \u8594  close\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Anything needing a pause-and-resume, the human-approval gate specifically needs this, n8n can trigger a workflow but isn't built for a multi-day paused-waiting-on-a-human state the way LangGraph's checkpointing is\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
